  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CU-Laos-IP3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Champasack University (CU) has established itself as a leader in climate resilience, renewable energy, sustainable agriculture, andinclusive development across southern Lao PDR. With a proven track record in implementing projects under regional frameworks like Mekong-Ganga and Lancang-Mekong Cooperation, CU has demonstrated strong capabilities in managing international partnerships and delivering impactful results. The university brings specialized expertise in community-based early warning systems, biofertilizers, biogas technology, and participatory forestry, ensuring that interventions are both technically sound and locally grounded.

In sustainable agriculture, CU has successfully promoted bio-fertilizers to combat soil degradation and implementedtree seedling nurseries to support ecological afforestation. In renewable energy, CU has pioneered fixed-dome biogas digesters across 10 districts in Champasak Province, while its research on rural energy transitions has informed national policies. The university has also made significant contributions to water resource management, designing irrigation systems that enhance agricultural productivity and foster cross-bordercollaboration. CU&#x2019;s work in climate adaptation includes developing community-based hydrometeorological monitoring systems and conducting vulnerability assessments in Salavan province, which have strengthened local resilience to floods and droughts. Additionally, the university has advanced sustainable fisheries in the 4000 Islands regionand facilitated community-led tourism development under the Lancang-Mekong Cooperation framework. With strong multidisciplinary expertise, deep community trust, and a robust logistical infrastructure, CU is well-equipped to coordinate field activities, lead training programs, and engage local stakeholders. Its active role in regional cooperation platforms and commitment to gender and social inclusion further enhance its ability to drive sustainable, scalable outcomes. By leveraging its technical knowledge, policy influence, and grassroots connections, CU is a vital partner in ensuring the success and long-term impact of development initiatives in the Mekong region.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="80">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Champasak University</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The University was established according to the Prime Minister&apos;s Decree No. 214/Nya, dated 28/11/2002
In accordance with the education strategy plan of the Ministry of Education and Sports aimed at strengthening higher education to meet the demands of socio-economic development, Champasak National University was established according to Prime Minister&apos;s Decree No. 214/Nya, dated 28/11/2002 and was renamed Champasak University according to Prime Minister&apos;s Decree No. 35/Nya, dated 07/05/2004. After that,the leadership teamat various levels along with the staff, teachers focused all their wisdom in the development to make this university grow day by day.

The vision is to develop Champasak University into a center for education, scientific research andquality technical services, a green institution and connected to the environment in the south of Lao PDR, regionally and internationally.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
